desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Use JSTL Escaping"
	title_zh: "检测到Use JSTL Escaping",
	type: vuln
	level: middle
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-use-jstl-escaping"
	risk: "xss"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `use-jstl-escaping` (/tmp/semgrep-rules/java/lang/security/audit/xss/jsp/use-jstl-escaping.yaml).
Original message: Detected an Expression Language segment in a tag that does not escape output. This is dangerous because if any data in this expression can be controlled externally, it is a cross-site scripting vulnerability. Instead, use the 'out' tag from the JSTL taglib to escape this expression. See https://www.tutorialspoint.com/jsp/jstl_core_out_tag.htm for more information.

CWE: CWE-116: Improper Encoding or Escaping of Output
References:
- https://www.tutorialspoint.com/jsp/jstl_core_out_tag.htm
- https://stackoverflow.com/a/4948856
- https://stackoverflow.com/a/3180202

False-positive hardening: ignore ${...} inside scriptlets and single-quoted JS strings inside tags.
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review the flagged code and follow the framework's secure coding guidance: use safe APIs, escape output, and avoid hardcoded credentials.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.jsp": <<<POS
<input value="${param.foo}" />
POS
	"safefile://neg.jsp": <<<NEG
<c:out value="${param.foo}" />
<button onClick="applyPermissionChanges('${id}')">go</button>
<a href="javascript:viewUser(\'${userId}\');">u</a>
<%=LanguageUtil.get(pageContext, "msg", "${owners}")%>
NEG
)

${*.jsp}.pattern_regex_not(/<(?![A-Za-z0-9]+:out)[^>\n]*\$\{[^}\n]*\}[^>\n]*>/, /'\$\{[^}\n]*\}'/, /\\'\$\{[^}\n]*\}\\'/, /javascript:[^>\n]*\$\{/, /<%[=!]?[^%]*\$\{/) as $p0
$p0 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Use JSTL Escaping",
	title_zh: "检测到Use JSTL Escaping",
	message: "Use JSTL Escaping",
}
